    "result_text": "I didn't change any code, because the create audit line already does what you asked for.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:166`), the `AUDIT` line already logs `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`. They sit next to the fields it logged before: `id`, `customerCode`, `region`, `checkDigit`, `registrationDate` and `membershipPoints`. Both values come from the same `OwnerMapper` methods that fill in the API response, so the log and the response match.\n\nHere is a real line from the test run:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11, customerCode=NSW-16E6609E, region=NSW, membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26, checkDigit=8, registrationDate=2026-10-14, membershipPoints=3, membershipLevel=2\n```\n\n**Tests:** I ran `./mvnw test` and all 17 tests passed (BUILD SUCCESS). That includes the new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber`. It creates an owner, fetches it back, and checks that the audit line contains that owner's `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`.\n\nIf you expected a different log format, such as different field order or names, tell me what you want and I'll change it.",
